   "subject": "Global variables in nimbleFunction",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Happy New Year everyone!</div><div><br></div><div>I was just wondering if there is a simple way to define and use global constants that can be used in compiled user-defined nimbleFunctions.  For example, the following wouldn&#39;t work:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#800\"># Define a global constant</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>MEANINGOFLIFE </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">42</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Define a user-defined function</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>myFunctionA </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> nimbleFunction</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    run </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Parameter list here...</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Some code that uses MEANINGOFLIFE</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>because under compilation the MEANINGOFLIFE is not defined and resolved (as it exists in an R environment only).</div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;ve instead been doing the following:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#800\"># Define a function that does nothing except return the global constant</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>meaningOfLife </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> nimbleFunction</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    run </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># No parameters</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        returnType</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">integer</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        </span><span style=\"color:#008\">return</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">42</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Define a user-defined function</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>myFunctionA </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> nimbleFunction</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    run </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>         </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Parameter list here...</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>         </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Some code that calls the global constant function</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>         meaningOfLife</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>But this seems a bit clunky and maybe I&#39;m missing an obvious easier way.<br><br>Thanks for any help you can give.<br><br>Joe<br></div></div>"
    ]
